Upstream-PR: build and publish a riscv64 binding
Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown
Upstream-Base: v1.3.3 (8a576d2f)
Upstream-Files: packages/rolldown/package.json, .github/workflows/reusable-release-build.yml

Why: rolldown has no riscv64 binding. The loader in packages/rolldown/src/binding.cjs
already knows how to load one (it probes @rolldown/binding-linux-riscv64-gnu before
falling back), so the only thing missing is a build that produces it.

What: the target joins napi.targets, which makes napi pre-publish emit
@rolldown/binding-linux-riscv64-gnu next to the other 16 platform packages and add
it to the wrapper's optionalDependencies. The release workflow gains one matrix
entry, built natively on a self-hosted riscv64 runner: GitHub hosts no riscv64
runner, and cross-building this workspace under emulation costs more than the build
itself. The runs-on line becomes sequential so every other entry keeps its hosted
runner unchanged.

Note: no source change is needed, and no other architecture starts being built
differently - the increment is one target, one matrix row, one runs-on fallback.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/reusable-release-build.yml b/.github/workflows/reusable-release-build.yml
index f4e60697..859d02a9 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/reusable-release-build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/reusable-release-build.yml
@@ -76,13 +76,21 @@ jobs:
             target: powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu
             build: vp run ci:build-release-binding --target powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu --use-napi-cross
 
+          # riscv64 is built on a native runner: GitHub hosts none, and a cross
+          # build of this workspace under emulation is slower than the build itself.
+          - os: ubuntu-latest
+            runs-on: [self-hosted, linux, riscv64]
+            target: riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu
+            build: vp run ci:build-release-binding --target riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu
+
           - os: ubuntu-latest
             target: wasm32-wasip1-threads
             build: |
               vp run --filter rolldown build-binding:wasi:release
 
     name: Build ${{ matrix.target }}
-    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
+    # Sequential runs-on: an entry overrides the hosted runner it would default to.
+    runs-on: ${{ matrix['runs-on'] || matrix.os }}
     steps:
       - uses: taiki-e/checkout-action@7d1e50e93dc4fb3bba58f85018fadf77898aee8b # v1.4.2
 
diff --git a/packages/rolldown/package.json b/packages/rolldown/package.json
